<h1>{`Sponsor`}</h1>
<p class="lede">{`Beautiful Eyes is a solo, spare-time project -- no company, no funding round, just time carved out around a day job. If it has been useful to you, sponsoring keeps that time coming.`}</p>

<div class="sponsor-row">
  <div class="sponsor-qr">
    <img src="/upi.jpeg" alt="UPI payment QR code" />
    <span class="sponsor-caption">{`scan with any UPI app -- Google Pay, PhonePe, Paytm, BHIM, or your bank's own app`}</span>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>{`How it works`}</h2>
<ol>
  <li>{`Open any UPI-enabled app on your phone.`}</li>
  <li>{`Scan the QR code above.`}</li>
  <li>{`Enter any amount and send it.`}</li>
</ol>
<p>{`That's it -- no account to create, no subscription, no third-party platform sitting in between.`}</p>

<h2>{`Why sponsor`}</h2>
<ul>
  <li>{`There is no company or investor behind this project -- every hour spent on it competes directly with everything else in a day.`}</li>
  <li>{`Sponsorship funds exactly the kind of work that is easy to defer otherwise: fixing real bugs found by actually dogfooding the framework (several were found and fixed while building this very docs site), writing the documentation contributors actually need, and building out features like the component system and @for's keyed reconciliation.`}</li>
  <li>{`It keeps the framework free and open source, with no paid tier, ever.`}</li>
</ul>

<h2>{`Other ways to help`}</h2>
<p>{`Can't sponsor, or would rather not? These help just as much:`}</p>
<ul>
  <li>{`Star the repo, or share it with someone who might find it interesting.`}</li>
  <li>{`Open an issue for any bug you hit -- see the Contributing tab for how the codebase fits together.`}</li>
  <li>{`Send a pull request.`}</li>
</ul>

<div class="callout">
  <span class="callout-title">{`Thank you`}</span>
  <p>{`Every bit of support -- a coffee, a star, an issue, a pull request -- genuinely helps keep this going. Thank you.`}</p>
</div>
